  "summary": "The identified studies apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to the task of estimating agricultural yield. Reported performance varies, with Gupta et al. (2024) achieving the highest accuracy of 0.89 on the CellLife dataset [V0039]. Fischer et al. (2023) report an F1 score of 0.82 on LedgerGuard [V0038], while Haddad et al. (2025) report an MAE of 0.61 on ToxiBench [V0040]. El-Sayed et al. (2022) report an AUROC of 0.75 on AgriSat-4 [V0037]. For context, a non-gradient-boosting approach using self-attention encoder models achieved an F1 of 0.74 on ToxiBench [V0032].",
